        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.361,
            0.481,
            0.874,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take samples of sodium chloride, potassium iodide, barium chloride or any other salt from the science laboratory.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.362,
            0.511,
            0.739,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the physical state of these salts?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.362,
            0.526,
            0.874,
            0.555
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take a small amount of a sample on a metal spatula and heat directly on the flame (Fig. 3.7). Repeat with other samples.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.363,
            0.555,
            0.874,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What did you observe? Did the samples impart any colour to the flame? Do these compounds melt?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.371,
            0.583,
            0.873,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try to dissolve the samples in water, petrol and kerosene. Are they soluble?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.363,
            0.613,
            0.874,
            0.657
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Make a circuit as shown in Fig. 3.8 and insert the electrodes into a solution of one salt. What did you observe? Test the other salt samples too in this manner.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.381,
            0.656,
            0.874,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is your inference about the nature of these compounds?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
